1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,024
My hands stopped shaking the exact moment the heavy wool coat whispered my true name out loud.

2
00:00:06,324 --> 00:00:12,660
I never asked to inherit this cursed sewing machine or the dusty tailor shop left behind by my uncle.

3
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:19,416
Each time I fix a torn seam on this heavy coat, a piece of my own memory vanishes forever.

4
00:00:19,716 --> 00:00:26,004
I lost my first heartbreak while repairing the left sleeve. I couldn't even remember her face anymore.

5
00:00:26,304 --> 00:00:33,816
Greed whispered in my ear. I pulled tighter threads to fix the frayed collar and win back my lost youth.

6
00:00:34,116 --> 00:00:41,436
Suddenly, a silver pocket watch fell from the heavy lining, ticking backward with a deafening, metallic rhythm.

7
00:00:41,736 --> 00:00:47,952
Engraved on the back was my own handwriting, warning me to stop sewing before it was too late.

8
00:00:48,252 --> 00:00:55,116
I looked in the cracked mirror and saw a stranger staring back: younger, paler, and fading into dust.

9
00:00:55,416 --> 00:01:02,496
The coat was never an inheritance. It was a trap laid by the man I am slowly becoming.

10
00:01:02,796 --> 00:01:10,956
My fingers touched the final button, and the thread snapped, taking my entire existence into the silent dark.
